    "start": {
      "id": "start",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "Let's learn the basic language of powers.\n\nIn 2^4, the base is 2 and the index is 4. It means:\n\n2 × 2 × 2 × 2.\n\nThe index laws are shortcuts for patterns like this. We will see why each shortcut works before using it.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "concept_1"
        }
      ]
    },
    "concept_1": {
      "id": "concept_1",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "An index tells us how many times a base is multiplied by itself.\n\nFor example:\n\n3^4 = 3 × 3 × 3 × 3 = 81.\n\nDo not multiply the base by the exponent. 3^4 is not 3 × 4.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "q_1"
        }
      ]
    },
