    "q_5_remedy": {
      "id": "q_5_remedy",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "A common possible slip here is to use the right rule on the wrong structure.\n\nFor this question:\n\nWhich is equal to (2 × 5)^3?\n\nStart from this clue:\nThe exponent 3 applies to both factors.\n\nThen follow the second clue and solve only after the expression is rewritten correctly.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "q_5_retry"
        }
      ]
    },
    "q_5_retry_fix": {
      "id": "q_5_retry_fix",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "Let's repair the retry with its actual values.\n\n(3/4)^2 = 3^2/4^2.\n\nThe key is to identify the structure first, then apply the matching law.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
